  "description": "Planning Permission is sought for a single storey rear/ side extension, which constitutes a re-submission of exactly the same scheme that previously received permission (Reference: DC/17/002822), as the client now intends to build the extension.  The aim is that the extension will form attractive architectural addition to the property.  To this end, the following design considerations have been included within the scheme:\n• The extension is of a modest size and restricted to infilling the space to the side of the existing rear closet wing: it does not project beyond the line of the rear wall of the closet wing and retains a distance of 950mm between the side wall of the extension and the boundary line at no. 81 Blythe Vale.\n• Finishes/ materials have been selected that are sympathetic to the existing property and also provide a smart and contemporary feel, with clean lines: brickwork walls to match existing walls; powder coated aluminium folding/ sliding door frames; and powder coated sloping glazed panels between the extension side wall and the side wall of the existing closet wing.",
